     Update from V1.05 to V1.06



     ================( ISDN )====================

     A number of lines are converted to ISDN (including the BBS line)

     But all the numbers are unchanged !!!

     It was a little messy, because they programmed the wrong numbers
     in the DuoVox (A/B converter).

     The BBS is still reachable at +31-599-564696
     but still only at 14k4 baud (V32B/V42B).

     The only ISDN device is a 3COM/USrobotics courier internal ISDN/V34 modem
     in a Pentium 233 Mhz machine.
     It isn't mine but I have access to it, 64K baud to Aminet :)

     I hope the line is of better quality now, the last weeks
     I got some pathetic connects, like a connect at 4800 baud
     and then retraining step for step to 14k4.



     ================( RIP  )====================

     After the previous update was send I found a new file on
     Aminet in the BBS directory with loads of RIP screen and Icons.

     RIPGRAPHICSP_I.LHA   1MegaByte   (1002854 bytes)

     (NOT included in this archive ;)


     I includes some incredible things like a file of 240K which was
     a picture of an Amiga drawing with a color drawing of a
     female/robot over it. Not very practicale because it takes
     a little more then a minute to be transmitted on 28k8 but
     local it is very beautifull. Most screens were only a few KB.

     I made a command that showed all 98 screens one after each other
     on the BBS and it didn't crash ;)

     But a little drawback is that a number of screens use Icons,
     which are included but are only shown (very quickly) when
     they are already on your disk. So if you want users to see
     them .. they have to install them first. But there where some
     incredable icons .. like a sceen filling eagle.

     Also I found it contained some text about RIPscrip 2.0
     (layout.rip) which was finished like two years ago.
     Well at that time only the MS-Dos version was available.
     I thougth V1.54 was the last version because everyone
     used that one. The company has gone commercial with V1.54.

     From what I understand V2.00 is an extention of V1.54
     with digitized sound, hires true color JPEG images with
     scaling color mapping and image replacement in real time.

     <= start of little quote =>

     The selection of fonts  is virtually unlimited, because
     RIPscrip 2.0 can import Adobe(tm) Type 1 and TrueType(tm) fonts.
     RIPscrip 2.0 can dynamically integrate graphics, photos, and text.
     The new device-independent bitmap (BMP/DIB) icon format gives sysops
     cross-platform compatibility for their screens, so the screens
     will be virtually identical on both PC and Macintosh computers.

     <= end of little quote =>

     I don't have found any docs on RIPscrip V2.0 yet, but compaired
     with the previous version (V1.54) it has some very BIG extensions.

     Version 1.54 was all about simple drawing commands, saving and
     loading pieces of the screen to disk and rendering buttons.

     Added in 2.00 are things even JPEG viewers cant' do.
     I don't know if it is actually integrated in BBS programs
     but it would take an incredible amount of code, and the
     executable would grow very big.
     Also this would mean colleting and integrating third
     party source code because things as JPEG come as demo
     source code.

     But the biggest problem is the terminal and editor software.
     They are all for V1.54
     The only programs I'm aware of are the commercial PC and Mac
     terminals mentioned in the doc.

     Anyway .. the question is if anyone would use the new commands,
     because sending of digitized sound and pictures become
     neccesary (and actually making the screens).
     But an implementation of just V1.54 only is very usefull.
     Screens that follow the V2.00 specs should be rendered
     fine on the "other side" if it has an V2.00 spec terminal
     but on the local V1.54 compliant side only the new features
     are left out. Also I don't think my (OCS) A2000/A2630 is
     the right system for V2.00 because users will be waiting
     while my systems is still displaying the JPEG files, and it
     has no true color anyway.

     Has anyone played with the RIPscrip since the last update ??
     Has anyone encountered any problems ??
     Is anyone actually thinking of using it in their BBSes ? :)
     If no one is using it I will still be busy with getting
     everything compliant to V1.54 but won't be searching for
     the V2.00 specs.




     Utils:   BBS, TrionRM, menu
     Doors:   
     Cfg:



   -In the previous version the length of Message section names
    and Tag names could only be 29 characters. That was a
    problem if you wanted to make a longer description of a message
    section or if you gate newsgroups with a very long name.
    So in this version they can be 79 characters.
    The file section names are still 49 characters max.

    This change made it necessary to recompile all programs
    that use services of TrionRM. So I took this opertunity
    to remove a few variables in the MsgSection and FileSection
    code that aren't needed anymore.

 !! These changes mean that the recompiled programs are not
 !! compatible with V1.05 and earlier.
    You can not use these utils with earlier versions.
    So this update has no big changes to prevent it from
    being unuseable if there were new bugs.

    Recompiled are:

    TrionRM, BBS, TMP, AreaFix, TBU, CheckFileBase, FileEd,
    Freq, GuiMod, ListNodes, LOP, MailEd, MaintMod,
    PointScan, TrionAllFiles, TrionTick, UserEd,
    WaitNodes, RMCommander.


   -Buildin some E-mail support in Netmail message sections.

    If you have a netmail section you use for E-mail you can
    add an 'I' flag (for Internet) to the sections in the mailareas.cfg.

    When you write a message in this section the BBS will
    ask for an E-mail address and put a:
    "to: e-mail_address" line in the message at the position
    of the first line. 

    When you reply at a message in this section the message
    is scanned for a REPLYADDR kludge line and if an E-mail
    address is found it asks if you want to use that one or
    suply an other one.

#040  [NWI] 100  TRION:mail/   "[I-net] E-mail"   "E-Mail"  2:283/326.99

   -Added an option to make an E-mail section easier to use.

    When you put a line with GATE and a node number in the trion-X.cfg
    that node number will be used to send all messages to written
    in a message section with the I flag .. see above.


; Gate address for E-mail

GATE   2:284/324.999



   -Doubled the buffer in the menu compiler from 8K to 16K
    because it chocked on a menu command with 300 lines.
    (the one that displayed 98 RIP files)




   -Fixed a little problem with RIPscrip.
    The button code and the icon save/load code used the wrong
    text variable.
    So when you clicked on an a button sometimes the RIPcommand
    after the button was send after the command which was
    ment to send.
    And loading of buttons was a problem because the buttons
    couldn't be found.

   -Added some code to skip unknown RIPscrip commands.

   -Enhanced the baseline position with RIPscrip text.
    Also added the heigth of the character. I geuss the
    system RIP was developed on uses the the underside
    of characters as base instead of the upside.

   -I accidently made the maximum piece of the screen that
    can be grabbed a pixel to small.

   -Added a "Carriage return" (no "NewLine") after the clearscreen 
    code in the ClrScr menu command. Because if you would use a
    RIPscreen after that command the first line wouldn't
    be interpreted because RIP code should start at the beginning
    of a line (except when special codes are used).
    But the ANSI code isn't really needed because there are
    RIP codes to clear to screen .. but of cause not Clr command.


